{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they complained, etc., all the children of Israel, etc., all the congregation.</b> The reason for the doubled mention of the complainers, and also the change in the reference, is that the entirety of Israel was included among the complainers, but the words that came in argument were from the mouth of the general leadership of the congregation who were fit to speak in argument with Moses. And they stated the order of choosing evil: the first division — ״If only we had died in the land of Egypt״ — but this was impossible for them, since they had already left; and they chose an evil greater than it, that they should die in the wilderness, and this is within the realm of possibility, for He would cause them to die in the wilderness. Why does HaShem bring them to a worse level, to die by the sword and for their wives to be taken captive, etc.? And they concluded by saying <b>״Is it not better״</b> — meaning, if HaShem does not cause them to die in the wilderness, they agree to return to Egypt, since perhaps the Egyptians would not put them to death and their lives would be theirs as spoil. And they were not afraid lest HaShem decree upon them and cause them to die in the wilderness so that they would not reach Egypt — for this was in fact their desire, as they said: ״or in this wilderness״ etc."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:43.367434131Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}